<BaseLayout title='Home | damienrobson'>
  <h1>Making the web a better place for everyone.</h1>
  <p>
    Hi, I'm Damien, but you can call me Damo. I'm an accessibility specialist,
    and this is where I write about digital inclusion, practical design, and
    building a web that doesn't leave people behind.
  </p>
  <a href='/blog'>Read my ramblings here</a>

  <h2>Why I'm here</h2>
  <p>
    The web is one of the most powerful tools we have, but too often, it's built
    with barriers baked right in.
  </p>
  <p>
    I set up this site as a cosy corner of the internet to share thoughts on
    accessibility—the wins, the common pitfalls, and the simple shifts that make
    a huge difference for real people. Whether you're a developer, designer, or
    just curious about making digital spaces more inclusive, I'm glad you're
    here.
  </p>

  <div>
    <strong>Quick thought</strong>: Accessibility isn't a checklist to tick off
    at the end of a project; it's just good design from day one.
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
